NAME
       skopeo - inspect and copy container images in registries

SYNOPSIS
       skopeo [GLOBAL-OPTIONS] COMMAND [OPTIONS] ARGUMENTS

DESCRIPTION
       skopeo works with container images without pulling them into local
       storage and without running a container. Its best-known use is to look
       at an image while it is still in the registry: which tags exist, which
       labels it has, what user it runs as, which ports it exposes. That lets
       you choose the right image before you download it with podman pull.

       skopeo is part of the container-tools package on RHEL 9, together with
       podman and buildah. It reads the same registry login as podman, so after
       "podman login registry.lab.example.com" skopeo can reach that registry
       too.

       Images are named with a transport in front:
       docker://HOST/PATH:TAG is an image in a registry,
       containers-storage:NAME is an image in local podman storage,
       dir:/PATH is an image unpacked into a directory.

COMMANDS
       inspect docker://IMAGE
              Print the image's details as JSON: name, digest, the tags of the
              repository, creation date, architecture, labels and environment.

       list-tags docker://REPOSITORY
              Print the tags that exist for a repository.

       copy SOURCE DESTINATION
              Copy an image from one place to another, for example from a
              registry into local storage or into a directory.

       login REGISTRY, logout REGISTRY
              Log in to (or out of) a registry, as podman login does.

OPTIONS
       --creds USER:PASSWORD
              Use this user name and password for the registry instead of a
              saved login.

       -f, --format TEMPLATE
              With inspect, print only the parts named in a Go template, such
              as '{{.Labels}}'.

EXAMPLES
       Log in and look at an image before pulling it:

           podman login registry.lab.example.com
           skopeo inspect docker://registry.lab.example.com/ubi9/httpd-24

       List the tags of a repository:

           skopeo list-tags docker://registry.lab.example.com/ubi9/ubi

       Copy an image into local storage:

           skopeo copy docker://registry.lab.example.com/ubi9/ubi \
               containers-storage:registry.lab.example.com/ubi9/ubi

NOTES
       skopeo needs the transport in front of a registry image (docker://);
       without it, it reports an invalid source name.

FILES
       /etc/containers/registries.conf
              Registries that are searched, blocked or allowed without TLS.

       ${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR}/containers/auth.json
              Saved registry logins.

SEE ALSO
       podman(1), buildah(1), containers-registries.conf(5)
